DANGLING POINTER:
- Pointer which is pointing to deleted memory.
- If we dereference, it will end up with segmentation fault mostly but sometimes it ends up as a garbage value(for huge program) both causes error as "undefined behaviour".

STATIC(Keyword):
- Static helps to allocate memory in data segment. It stores the memory until we write return 0; in main block.
- Data segment is divided into two:
1) DS (Initialized)
2) BSS (UnInitialized)

- Memory is allocated in compile time only.
- syntax:
static datatype variable;
eg:
static int n;
- if we assign any value to variable, its okay. if not by default it is considers as "zero".
- It is a local variable.
- It does not store the value of another variable addresses or values. It is an error.

eg:
